---
// Figure 3: MOVED against ASK, as a client meets them.
import SimFigure from '../shared/SimFigure.astro';
import Choice from '../shared/Choice.astro';
import './cluster.css';
interface Props { number: number }
const { number } = Astro.props;
---
<SimFigure number={number} id="cluster-redirect" title="MOVED and ASK: a slot that has moved, and one that is moving" controls="steps"
  caption="A sequence of steps, not a timed simulation. Every reply shown is one I received from a three-primary Redis 8.10.3 cluster on my laptop, while moving slot 12456 key by key with CLUSTER SETSLOT and MIGRATE; node C is the server on port 7197 and node A the one on 7195. Left out: how a client library hides all of this behind one call.">
  <Choice slot="params" name="case" label="The slot" value="moved"
    options={[{ value: 'moved', label: 'has moved (MOVED)' }, { value: 'ask', label: 'is moving (ASK)' }]} />
  <Fragment slot="text">
    <p>A slot that has moved: the client sends GET product:42 to node C, which its slot map names for slot 12456. Node C no longer owns the slot and replies MOVED 12456 with node A's address. The client updates its map, ideally reloading it whole with CLUSTER SHARDS or the older CLUSTER SLOTS, resends the GET to node A and gets the value. Later requests for the slot go straight to node A.</p>
    <p>A slot that is moving: node C still owns slot 12456 and is copying its keys to node A one at a time. A GET for a key not yet copied is answered by node C as usual. A GET for product:42, already copied, gets ASK 12456 with node A's address, and so would a GET for a key that was never there. The client sends ASKING and then the GET to node A, which answers; ASKING lasts for one command, and the client leaves its map unchanged. An MGET whose keys are split between the two nodes gets TRYAGAIN and must be retried once the slot has moved.</p>
  </Fragment>
</SimFigure>
<script>
  import { switchSequence } from './switch-sequence.mjs';
  import { redirectSpecs } from './sequences.mjs';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-figure-id="cluster-redirect"]').forEach(root => switchSequence(root, redirectSpecs, 'case'));
</script>
